.NET Developer Verbal Interview Preparation

1.  Tell me about yourself. Sample: My name is Jafor Sadik Tutul. I am a
    Software Engineer with over 4 years of experience developing web
    applications using ASP.NET Core, C#, Entity Framework Core, SQL
    Server, and REST APIs. I have experience with layered architecture,
    JWT authentication, Repository and Unit of Work patterns, and
    responsive front-end development. Recently I’ve also been learning
    React.

2.  Explain your current project. Mention:

-   Project name
-   Purpose
-   Technologies
-   Your responsibilities

3.  Layered Architecture Presentation -> API -> Business/Manager ->
    Repository/Data Access -> Database Benefits:

-   Easy maintenance
-   Loose coupling
-   Better testing
-   Reusability

4.  Repository Pattern Abstracts database CRUD operations into
    repositories.

5.  Unit of Work Coordinates multiple repositories with one DbContext
    and SaveChanges().

6.  Repository vs Unit of Work Repository = CRUD Unit of Work =
    Transaction + SaveChanges()

7.  Dependency Injection Provides dependencies from outside the class.
    Benefits:

-   Loose coupling
-   Easier testing

8.  REST API GET = Read POST = Create PUT = Update DELETE = Delete PATCH
    = Partial Update

9.  PUT vs PATCH PUT updates the whole object. PATCH updates selected
    fields.

10. JWT Authentication Header + Payload + Signature Login -> Validate ->
    Generate Token -> Client sends token -> Server validates.

11. Entity Framework Core ORM with LINQ, Change Tracking, Migrations.

12. Database First vs Code First Database First: Existing DB generates
    models. Code First: Models generate database.

13. LINQ Query data using C#.

14. IQueryable vs IEnumerable IQueryable executes in SQL. IEnumerable
    executes in memory.

15. Know: First() FirstOrDefault() Single()

16. SQL Topics DELETE vs TRUNCATE vs DROP JOINs GROUP BY HAVING
    ROW_NUMBER CTE Stored Procedure View Function Trigger Indexes

17. Normalization 1NF 2NF 3NF

18. SQL Optimization

-   Indexes
-   Avoid SELECT *
-   Proper JOINs
-   Execution Plans
-   Pagination

19. async/await Non-blocking asynchronous programming.

20. Task vs Thread Task = High-level abstraction. Thread = OS thread.

21. SOLID S - Single Responsibility O - Open Closed L - Liskov I -
    Interface Segregation D - Dependency Inversion

22. React Basics Components Props State Hooks React Router Axios

23. React vs Angular React = Library Angular = Full Framework

24. CORS Allows cross-origin API requests.

25. HTTP Status Codes 200 OK 201 Created 400 Bad Request 401
    Unauthorized 403 Forbidden 404 Not Found 500 Server Error

26. Git Workflow Clone Branch Commit Push Pull Request Merge

27. Difficult Problem Solved Prepare one real example from your work.

28. Why do you want to join? Mention learning, modern stack,
    contribution, growth.

29. Why should we hire you? Highlight .NET, EF Core, SQL Server, REST
    API, teamwork, learning ability.

30. HR Questions

-   Strengths
-   Weaknesses
-   Why leaving current company
-   Five-year goal
-   Salary expectation
-   Working under pressure

Questions to Ask Interviewer - What projects will I work on? - How is
the team structured? - Code review process? - Learning opportunities?

Interview Tips - Speak confidently. - Use simple examples. - If unsure,
admit it and explain how you’d learn. - Focus on projects you’ve
personally built.
